2026-11-10T20:47:23.0115550Z ### Resources: CPU per byte and scaling, the `wikidata` corpus
2026-11-10T20:47:23.0116074Z 
2026-11-10T20:47:23.0118117Z **Assessment:** No change detected on the four measures at this run's precision (every interval holds no change; not a proof that nothing changed).
2026-11-10T20:47:23.0119186Z 
2026-11-10T20:47:23.0121645Z **CPU per byte** is the process's CPU (every thread, user + sys) over the output. **Amplification** is that at N threads over the same build's at 1, paired by round: 1× is no extra CPU for the same bytes, and above it the work costs more as threads are added (stalls, sharing, synchronisation; CPU counts a thread stalled on memory as running). **Efficiency** is the speedup over N. **Run-queue** is the threads' mean count runnable but not running.
2026-11-10T20:47:23.0123215Z 
2026-11-10T20:47:23.0123775Z | threads: placement | base MB/s | base CPU ns/B | base amplification | base efficiency | head MB/s | head CPU ns/B | head amplification | head efficiency | amplification, head over base |
2026-11-10T20:47:23.0124514Z |---|--:|--:|--:|--:|--:|--:|--:|--:|--:|
2026-11-10T20:47:23.0125166Z | 1: pinned to CPU 1 | 402 | 2.50 | 1 | – | 400 | 2.51 | 1 | – |  |
